# Generated by the pipeline. Reproducible from the templates, config/seed.json and
# the deterministic per-(program, template, variant) seeds, so none of it belongs
# in git.

# pipelines/generate.py output
shards/

# pipelines/progress.py output, rewritten on every generation run.
# `progress/*` rather than `progress/`, because git does not descend into an
# excluded *directory* -- a negation below it would never be consulted.
progress/*

# ...except the think ablation, which is a decision record rather than a
# regenerated report. Amendment §B fixes this path, `dataset_build.sh full`
# refuses while it reads NOT YET MEASURED, and a precondition whose evidence
# cannot be committed is a precondition every box has to re-satisfy alone and
# nobody can review. Found the hard way: the corpus validated clean on a
# second machine and the audit refused there for want of a file that could
# not have arrived. Same reasoning as gold_bar.jsonl at the foot of this file.
!progress/v3_think_ablation.md

# scripts/publish_dataset.py default output name
dataset_v2_*.json

# in-flight shard writes, before _finalize_all() renames them
*.jsonl.tmp

# eval/ab_eval.py working files. ab_results.json is a per-round measurement -- if
# you want to keep a round's numbers, copy it to a round-stamped name and track that.
eval/ab_tasks.jsonl
eval/ab_scores.jsonl
eval/ab_results.json

# verification/suite_overlap.py report, regenerated on every run
verification/suite_overlap.json

# publish/push_to_hub.py renders this from the corpus on every run; the template
# it is rendered from (dataset_card.md) is the tracked artifact.
publish/dataset_card_generated.md

# smoke-run scratch output
.smoke/

__pycache__/

# Deliberately tracked, despite being generated:
#   taxonomy/coverage.json  - the brief requires coverage tracked as data, not prose
#   goldbar/gold_bar.jsonl  - a measurement instrument; must be diffable and reviewable
#   progress/v3_think_ablation.md - the §B bake-off's verdict; the publish path
#                             gates on it, so it has to travel with the repo
